1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:03,330
[Characters, places and incidents
in this production]

2
00:00:03,330 --> 00:00:06,698
[are entirely fictitious.]

3
00:00:06,698 --> 00:00:10,004
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

4
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:02,080
And don't even think about
playing games with Sam or Lek.

5
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:04,720
I've been thinking about who I should seduce.

6
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,073
Ran!

7
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,430
So, do you hate her, or worry about her?

8
00:01:14,209 --> 00:01:15,790
Hang in there.

9
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:19,078
I'll make sure you and our child
can live comfortably and happily.

10
00:01:19,078 --> 00:01:20,240
Get rid of the child.

11
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:24,500
If you don't do it,
I'll do way worse things to your family.

12
00:01:27,343 --> 00:01:29,160
[Obstetrics and Gynecology Clinic]

13
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:30,480
What did you do?

14
00:01:33,252 --> 00:01:35,422
I had an abortion.

15
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:58,582
That's our child, Ran.

16
00:02:03,677 --> 00:02:06,801
Weren't you the one
who told me to do it in the first place?

17
00:02:08,206 --> 00:02:10,887
Why are you asking me now?

18
00:02:13,530 --> 00:02:15,720
How could you be so cruel?

19
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:19,360
I just want to choose
the best thing for myself.

20
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:22,320
I used to think you could provide for me,

21
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:25,120
but not anymore.

22
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:27,687
With that salary...

23
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:31,109
you can't even take care of yourself.

24
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,946
I don't want to talk about this here.

25
00:02:41,184 --> 00:02:42,844
It's embarrassing.

26
00:02:52,081 --> 00:02:53,941
- Talk nicely, dear.
- Yes.

27
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,696
Ran.

28
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:17,787
We should break up.

29
00:03:17,787 --> 00:03:21,900
You continue your studies,
and I'll try out for the national team.

30
00:03:23,356 --> 00:03:26,773
Not getting into a university
is just my bad luck.

31
00:03:26,773 --> 00:03:27,850
Ran...

32
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,366
Ran.

33
00:03:34,674 --> 00:03:36,162
It's okay.

34
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:38,480
We can have another child.

35
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,829
The problem is gone.

36
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:46,170
Let's not make another one.

37
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,405
You can sleep with me tonight,

38
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,480
but you have to wear a condom.

39
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,498
I don't want any more problems.

40
00:04:00,464 --> 00:04:03,400
Let tonight be our last night together,

41
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,120
and tomorrow,

42
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,620
we'll go our separate ways.

43
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,640
Problem?

44
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,500
If you want to have sex with me,

45
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:31,100
you don't have to use
wanting a child as an excuse.

46
00:04:31,100 --> 00:04:35,200
I understand that you have nothing left.

47
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:38,780
There is nothing I can get from you
but pleasure.

48
00:04:41,523 --> 00:04:44,048
When tonight is over,
we'll have to part ways.

49
00:04:44,975 --> 00:04:47,369
I can't stand this hardship anymore.

50
00:04:48,798 --> 00:04:51,509
A bright future is waiting for us.

51
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:57,520
Hey, what the hell is your problem, Ran?

52
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:59,720
You're the one with a problem, Yai!

53
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:02,626
Weren't you just acting like
you wanted to sleep with me?

54
00:05:02,626 --> 00:05:04,120
What did our child do wrong?

55
00:05:04,120 --> 00:05:06,800
They were wrong for being our child!

56
00:05:08,557 --> 00:05:10,837
Just accept...

57
00:05:10,837 --> 00:05:12,962
that we can't take care of them.

58
00:05:13,861 --> 00:05:15,819
I was the one carrying our child,

59
00:05:16,565 --> 00:05:17,913
not you.

60
00:05:19,539 --> 00:05:21,108
Let's get a divorce tomorrow.

61
00:05:22,355 --> 00:05:25,296
You still haven't taken
the documents back home,

62
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:29,772
so just get a divorce,
then take them all back at once.

63
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:31,765
Are you serious?

64
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,827
We all show our true colors
in times of hardship.

65
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,061
This, Yai,

66
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,265
is who I am.

67
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:42,038
You thought
you saw through me, didn't you?

68
00:05:49,524 --> 00:05:51,430
Is that really what you think?

69
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,316
Fine.

70
00:06:14,370 --> 00:06:16,316
Let's get a divorce tomorrow.

71
00:06:32,280 --> 00:06:35,411
Yai, I'm sorry.

72
00:06:55,741 --> 00:07:01,541
[Divorce Certificate]

73
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:21,160
As soon as I leave, there's trouble.
What happened?

74
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:23,333
That girl is vicious,

75
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:25,800
and Yai is stupid enough
to let her baby-trap him.

76
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:29,342
Are you insulting Yai
or my son for falling into a baby trap?

77
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,667
Mother!

78
00:08:30,667 --> 00:08:33,762
You shouldn't have
driven him away like that, Angkhana.

79
00:08:33,762 --> 00:08:35,480
I didn't drive him away!

80
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:39,660
I just wanted to teach him
that life isn't always beautiful.

81
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:46,280
Speak of the devil.

82
00:08:48,532 --> 00:08:49,706
Yai...

83
00:08:50,618 --> 00:08:52,970
What happened, dear?

84
00:08:54,922 --> 00:08:55,928
Huh?

85
00:08:56,657 --> 00:09:00,560
I told you that you'll come crawling back here.

86
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:01,840
What did she do to you?

87
00:09:01,840 --> 00:09:04,657
Stop, Angkhana! Silence!

88
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:11,353
What happened? Tell me, dear.

89
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:14,110
She killed my child.

90
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:22,040
She asked for a divorce,
because I have nothing.

91
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:24,103
Do you believe me now

92
00:09:24,103 --> 00:09:27,189
that she deliberately
got pregnant to baby-trap you?

93
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:30,540
Dear.

94
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:34,134
Is there any way I can help?

95
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:37,353
I don't want to be here.

96
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:42,087
I don't want anyone to know
about the mistakes I've made.

97
00:09:54,079 --> 00:09:56,329
I won't bring this up again.

98
00:09:57,387 --> 00:10:00,501
Let's start a new life, okay?

99
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:04,640
It's still not too late, okay?

100
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,980
[2013]

101
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,460
[2026]

102
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,440
No matter how much I hate you,

103
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,456
I still don't want you to get hurt.

104
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:24,970
Get well soon.

105
00:10:27,245 --> 00:10:29,246
How is Ran?

106
00:10:30,276 --> 00:10:31,706
Old chump?

107
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,644
He's the Executive Chairman
of the company Ran works for.

108
00:10:38,400 --> 00:10:40,230
You must be Danai, right?

109
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,316
Do you remember me?

110
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:47,746
Do you know Danai?
How do you two know each other?

111
00:10:48,656 --> 00:10:51,136
And why are you here with Ran?

112
00:10:53,592 --> 00:10:54,863
Come here.

113
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,011
Is she your sister?

114
00:10:58,011 --> 00:10:59,988
Yeah. Why?

115
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:05,660
Why are you blocking me? What happened to Ran?

116
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:12,199
Ran, I came to see you.

117
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,592
Her father died...

118
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,952
the same year her sister was born?

119
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:47,288
That's right. It was a bus accident.

120
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,819
I want the exact date of her father's death,

121
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:55,005
and her sister's birth certificate.

122
00:11:55,005 --> 00:11:58,160
That might be a bit difficult these days,

123
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:00,590
but I think I can do it.

124
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:09,800
Are you sure
Daran didn't continue her education?

125
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:10,903
I am, sir.

126
00:12:17,424 --> 00:12:19,075
"Daranee..."

127
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:24,095
Her nickname was "Dao."

128
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:30,720
[Sunthorn Phu Day 2027]

129
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:33,360
And the last scholarship recipient is...

130
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:36,700
Miss Daranee Kaewkaruna.

131
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:15,418
♪ Of your love, Mother, I am well aware ♪

132
00:13:15,418 --> 00:13:24,443
♪ And none among thousands shall ever compare ♪

133
00:13:24,443 --> 00:13:32,280
♪ To how you tended me
throughout day and night ♪

134
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:40,731
♪ Only in body must I now leave your side ♪

135
00:13:47,270 --> 00:13:50,400
I'll give you this as a reward, because...

136
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,176
you recited the verses so well. I like it.

137
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:58,080
Thank you, Madam Namthip.

138
00:13:58,080 --> 00:14:00,920
Can you tell me what is your name again?

139
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:04,684
My name is Daranee. My nickname is Dao.

140
00:14:04,684 --> 00:14:07,460
"Dara" means "stars,"

141
00:14:08,168 --> 00:14:10,680
and "Nee" means "woman."

142
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:11,960
Did I guess that right?

143
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:14,123
Exactly.

144
00:14:14,123 --> 00:14:15,640
I'm sorry.

145
00:14:15,640 --> 00:14:19,740
It's okay. I like kids who are
comfortable being themselves.

146
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:23,933
Dao, I really want you...

147
00:14:23,933 --> 00:14:27,180
to come recite the verses for me at my house.

148
00:14:28,236 --> 00:14:30,808
I can give you some pocket money.

149
00:14:30,808 --> 00:14:33,142
I'm all alone at home.

150
00:14:33,142 --> 00:14:35,520
Having kids visit me sometimes

151
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:39,360
would help ease
this old woman's loneliness a lot.

152
00:14:40,736 --> 00:14:42,400
Can I be honest?

153
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:43,667
Of course.

154
00:14:43,667 --> 00:14:47,880
I do want the money
because my family is struggling.

155
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:50,790
But my older sister won't let me find a job,

156
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:54,880
because it might affect my studies,
but I still want to help her.

157
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,880
Then that's fine, dear.

158
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:58,103
I'll go.

159
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:03,120
If you want to go, just call me.

160
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,280
I'll have a car pick you up.

161
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:08,640
Well, is tomorrow okay?

162
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:11,920
My tutoring school canceled the last class.

163
00:15:12,907 --> 00:15:16,719
I really don't want to say that I need money.

164
00:15:27,789 --> 00:15:30,992
Daran's father died
shortly after I went to the US.

165
00:15:32,977 --> 00:15:35,480
If Daranee really is Duean's daughter,

166
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:37,860
then Duean must have been pregnant back then.

167
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:46,032
What about Daranee's birth certificate?

168
00:15:50,024 --> 00:15:51,274
Here.

169
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:57,710
[Birth Certificate]
[Ms. Daranee Kaewkaruna]

170
00:15:57,710 --> 00:15:59,710
[Third child]

171
00:15:59,710 --> 00:16:01,720
[Mother: Mrs. Dueanchan Kaewkaruna]

172
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:03,700
[Father: Mr. Chaisak Kaewkaruna]

173
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,055
No...

174
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:14,787
Your job is done.

175
00:16:14,787 --> 00:16:16,690
I'll transfer your final payment.

176
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:19,630
- Thank you, sir.
- Wait.

177
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:31,099
Take these documents back with you.

178
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:38,342
Okay. If you're not using these,
may I dispose of them?

179
00:16:47,737 --> 00:16:49,683
What were you thinking?

180
00:17:14,274 --> 00:17:15,493
Well...

181
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:19,010
The doctor said your injury
wasn't too severe.

182
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,800
I'll let you rest until you recover.

183
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:24,900
After you leave the hospital...

184
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,500
Wait.

185
00:18:08,666 --> 00:18:10,612
How am I supposed to think

186
00:18:12,534 --> 00:18:15,174
about my fiancé watching over
a security guard like this?

187
00:18:48,555 --> 00:18:51,800
Oh, Ms. Ran! Are you feeling better now?

188
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,520
Mr. Yai told me...

189
00:18:53,520 --> 00:18:56,790
to let you get plenty of rest
and not to call you.

190
00:18:56,790 --> 00:18:58,080
I'm all better now.

191
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,820
How many stitches did you get?

192
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,312
Two.

193
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Mr. Yai was really shocked,
so he rushed you to the hospital.

194
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:12,120
Mr. Yai... may appear a bit harsh,

195
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:15,215
- but he's actually kind. Not mean at all.
- He is sometimes.

196
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:18,160
He's not fierce.

197
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,600
But he doesn't back down.

198
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:22,365
Boy, why do you have to make it worse?

199
00:19:22,365 --> 00:19:25,440
- Right? I should be quiet, Dad?
- Dad? My ass!

200
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:28,320
- Chief.
- Say that again, and I'll kick your ass!

201
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:33,600
It's nothing. Just a father and son bickering,
that's all.

202
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:36,480
- I ran out of coffee. Make me some.
- Yes.

203
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,084
Ran...

204
00:20:10,840 --> 00:20:12,770
I came to visit you a few days ago.

205
00:20:13,390 --> 00:20:15,050
But Yai was taking care of you.

206
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,746
Thanks for visiting me.

207
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,793
I actually wanted to stay with you,

208
00:20:21,910 --> 00:20:23,386
because I was so worried.

209
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:27,880
You've done so much for me already.
Don't worry about me.

210
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:31,600
Of course I'm worried about you.
Because when I was struggling,

211
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,332
you helped me

212
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:36,308
and changed my life.

213
00:20:38,635 --> 00:20:40,895
So when you're struggling,

214
00:20:40,895 --> 00:20:42,760
or you're sick,

215
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,582
I want to be there for you.

216
00:20:46,511 --> 00:20:48,316
Thank you so much, Mr. Lek,

217
00:20:49,240 --> 00:20:51,472
for all the encouragement and everything.

218
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,760
Then let me...

219
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,600
treat you to lunch one last time.

220
00:20:58,144 --> 00:20:59,560
Alright.

221
00:20:59,560 --> 00:21:01,363
What would you like to eat?

222
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,035
I'm fine with anything.

223
00:21:09,105 --> 00:21:12,828
Hello, Ms. Natasha. How can we help you?

224
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,722
Looks great, doesn't it?

225
00:21:24,640 --> 00:21:26,141
It really does.

226
00:21:35,494 --> 00:21:36,774
Hello.

227
00:21:38,455 --> 00:21:39,755
This is Nana.

228
00:21:40,450 --> 00:21:44,205
Meet me at the executive parking
lot after work. Don't make me wait.

229
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:52,626
Is something wrong?

230
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,408
It's nothing.

231
00:21:58,239 --> 00:22:01,000
Okay... Then, shall we?

232
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,839
This way, please, Ms. Natasha.

233
00:22:20,625 --> 00:22:21,970
Sit down.

234
00:22:40,193 --> 00:22:41,561
Would you like to order?

235
00:22:43,576 --> 00:22:45,120
No, thank you.

236
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:46,320
It's on me.

237
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:49,615
Don't worry about the money.

238
00:22:50,200 --> 00:22:51,400
I'll pass.

239
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,840
Just tell me what you wanted.

240
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:03,120
Please, get to it.
I have business to attend to.

241
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:14,808
What business

242
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:17,964
could someone like you possibly have?

243
00:23:19,640 --> 00:23:21,600
I have side hustles.

244
00:23:22,785 --> 00:23:23,840
Wait...

245
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:25,680
Are you a security guard

246
00:23:26,875 --> 00:23:28,660
and a prostitute?

247
00:23:30,914 --> 00:23:32,400
Just get to the point.

248
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:34,080
Otherwise, I'm leaving.

249
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:35,336
Sit down.

250
00:23:37,560 --> 00:23:39,945
Look around you.

251
00:23:43,626 --> 00:23:45,720
Everyone who dines here

252
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:48,120
has high social status.

253
00:23:48,120 --> 00:23:50,240
They're all VIP guests.

254
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:53,369
Including Yai.

255
00:24:06,462 --> 00:24:08,102
Let me ask you,

256
00:24:09,626 --> 00:24:12,000
do you think you belong here?

257
00:24:12,920 --> 00:24:15,427
Do you think you can afford to eat here?

258
00:24:19,310 --> 00:24:22,800
Both Yai and I are surrounded by these people,

259
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:25,055
people of the same social standing

260
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,375
and from the same social circles.

261
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,935
We should just keep to ourselves.
You understand, right?

262
00:24:38,961 --> 00:24:40,486
Yes.

263
00:24:40,486 --> 00:24:44,560
Yai's life and mine
aren't what they were back in high school.

264
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:49,379
You don't even deserve to be our friend,
or even our acquaintance.

265
00:24:49,379 --> 00:24:50,860
Look behind you.

266
00:24:52,780 --> 00:24:56,479
That man is the son of the Minister of Tourism.

267
00:24:58,578 --> 00:25:00,112
And over there...

268
00:25:00,745 --> 00:25:03,151
is the grandson of a hotel owner.

269
00:25:03,896 --> 00:25:05,106
And right there...

270
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:09,300
is Mrs. Ruenrom, the Prime Minister's wife.

271
00:25:10,240 --> 00:25:12,620
Just give it to me straight.

272
00:25:13,560 --> 00:25:16,886
Yai and I aren't who we were in high school,

273
00:25:17,720 --> 00:25:20,080
when we met people of all classes.

274
00:25:20,080 --> 00:25:21,450
Now we live among people...

275
00:25:21,450 --> 00:25:24,680
of the same social standing
and from the same social circles.

276
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:26,485
We don't mingle.

277
00:25:26,485 --> 00:25:28,885
You shouldn't waste your time. Understand?

278
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:32,600
- Yes.
- Good.

279
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:36,000
I don't know why you and Yai broke up.

280
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,815
But all this time,
while you two have been apart,

281
00:25:38,815 --> 00:25:41,207
I've always been by his side.

282
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:47,286
Yai and I got engaged
while we were in the US.

283
00:25:51,479 --> 00:25:55,897
I don't know if you have any ulterior motive
for choosing to work at Yai's company.

284
00:25:55,897 --> 00:25:59,600
But Yai is one of the country's top executives.

285
00:25:59,600 --> 00:26:01,520
You really think he'd want

286
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:05,440
someone like you as his wife?

287
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:07,725
What about his mother?

288
00:26:07,725 --> 00:26:10,012
Will she let you use his last name?

289
00:26:10,680 --> 00:26:12,875
You're not as pretty or pure,

290
00:26:12,875 --> 00:26:15,775
and you don't look the same as
you did in school anymore.

291
00:26:17,320 --> 00:26:20,645
Stop being so full of yourself
and wasting your time.

292
00:26:22,811 --> 00:26:24,701
- Are you done?
- No.

293
00:26:26,238 --> 00:26:28,720
Between a one-year emotional relationship

294
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:32,296
and a ten-year relationship,
both physical and emotional,

295
00:26:32,296 --> 00:26:35,326
which do you think is more solid?

296
00:26:38,867 --> 00:26:41,440
If you're so sure yours is,

297
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:43,760
you wouldn't need to
tell me all this, would you?

298
00:26:45,100 --> 00:26:47,741
Unless you're feeling insecure.

299
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:54,880
One more thing.

300
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:57,116
I just handed in my resignation.

301
00:27:24,649 --> 00:27:26,566
Hello.

302
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:35,632
- Take those off and put on the slippers.
- Yes.

303
00:27:42,320 --> 00:27:44,742
Whoa.

304
00:27:46,520 --> 00:27:48,755
I'm getting goosebumps.

305
00:27:48,755 --> 00:27:50,220
Did you see a ghost?

306
00:27:50,220 --> 00:27:56,120
No, I mean, I'm so excited to see your house.
I got goosebumps.

307
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:58,950
That's good, then. Alright, let's get inside.

308
00:27:58,950 --> 00:28:01,677
Have some snacks
before you read a book to me.

309
00:28:01,677 --> 00:28:03,121
- Yes.
- Go.

310
00:28:10,967 --> 00:28:12,426
Hey!

311
00:28:13,418 --> 00:28:15,160
Hey!

312
00:28:15,160 --> 00:28:16,440
Hey!

313
00:28:19,760 --> 00:28:22,185
Have you two met before?

314
00:28:22,185 --> 00:28:23,540
Yes.

315
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:24,800
Let me speak.

316
00:28:25,440 --> 00:28:29,760
Alex is that chump's relative...
not a security guard.

317
00:28:29,760 --> 00:28:31,040
Liar!

318
00:28:31,040 --> 00:28:33,170
Who... Who is "that chump"?

319
00:28:33,170 --> 00:28:35,280
That chump is Yai.

320
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,740
And I wasn't lying.

321
00:28:36,740 --> 00:28:39,660
No one asked me
what my relationship with the Chairman was.

322
00:28:42,018 --> 00:28:45,465
And I really did work as a security guard.
I wasn't just pretending.

323
00:28:45,465 --> 00:28:47,960
You have a house, so why do you live in a dorm?

324
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:51,320
My music disturbs Grandma.
So I come back sometimes.

325
00:28:51,320 --> 00:28:52,720
Really?

326
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:55,220
Yes. Anything else?

327
00:29:02,182 --> 00:29:09,280
♪ She cried out, heartbroken ♪

328
00:29:09,280 --> 00:29:17,034
♪ Oh, how to oppose this cruel fate ♪

329
00:29:17,034 --> 00:29:23,980
♪ And the truth was finally told ♪

330
00:29:24,682 --> 00:29:31,580
♪ That you are not his flesh and blood, ♪
♪ thus his enmity ♪

331
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:37,280
Doesn't she look like me when I was younger?

332
00:29:37,880 --> 00:29:40,080
Very much so.

333
00:29:40,080 --> 00:29:42,341
That's why I like her.

334
00:29:42,341 --> 00:29:46,645
How could this be a coincidence?
Hey, she also has an amazing voice.

335
00:29:47,309 --> 00:29:49,536
They are both amazing.

336
00:29:51,981 --> 00:29:53,520
Both...

337
00:29:53,520 --> 00:29:56,239
Daran, Yai's girlfriend.

338
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:09,000
Alex, don't tell Ran that I work here.

339
00:30:10,040 --> 00:30:12,355
- Promise?
- I promise.

340
00:30:12,355 --> 00:30:13,960
My...

341
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:16,877
You've already got one foot in jail, Mr. Lek.

342
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:22,585
Kids these days are so slutty.

343
00:30:22,585 --> 00:30:24,797
They come to your house just to seduce you.

344
00:30:25,560 --> 00:30:27,297
Is she your friend?

345
00:30:31,426 --> 00:30:34,414
Excuse me. I'm tired.

346
00:30:41,297 --> 00:30:43,400
I thought she was your mom, Alex.

347
00:30:43,400 --> 00:30:45,060
No, she is Yai's mother.

348
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:48,380
No wonder they act so similar.

349
00:30:49,726 --> 00:30:51,846
But she's even cruder.

350
00:30:51,846 --> 00:30:53,760
Come on, time to go home.

351
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:56,892
And don't forget to come here as we agreed.
You stingy kid.

352
00:30:56,892 --> 00:30:58,820
Well, I'm not rich like you.

353
00:30:58,820 --> 00:31:01,310
If I want something, I have to work for it.

354
00:31:01,310 --> 00:31:03,020
I'll go now. Goodbye.

355
00:31:35,552 --> 00:31:37,052
Grandma.

356
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,713
Lek...

357
00:31:43,160 --> 00:31:44,672
Is everything alright?

358
00:31:45,560 --> 00:31:48,507
There's something I've never told you

359
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:52,436
since Yai asked me

360
00:31:52,436 --> 00:31:58,173
to forget everything that happened between Yai

361
00:31:58,173 --> 00:32:00,984
and a girl named Daran.

362
00:32:03,452 --> 00:32:05,432
Do you know her?

363
00:32:07,185 --> 00:32:08,340
Yes.

364
00:32:08,973 --> 00:32:10,747
What is she like?

365
00:32:15,010 --> 00:32:16,200
She's talented,

366
00:32:17,072 --> 00:32:18,278
smart,

367
00:32:19,080 --> 00:32:20,359
and kind.

368
00:32:20,967 --> 00:32:22,974
Was she Yai's girlfriend?

369
00:32:23,880 --> 00:32:24,906
Yes.

370
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:28,888
Then did you know that Yai got her pregnant?

371
00:32:32,716 --> 00:32:35,600
But then she had an abortion

372
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:37,840
and broke up with Yai.

373
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:45,827
Don't tell Angkhana about this just yet.

374
00:32:46,953 --> 00:32:48,349
Keep it secret.

375
00:32:50,077 --> 00:32:52,794
There's something I want to know.

376
00:32:54,399 --> 00:32:56,622
I have to know the truth.

377
00:32:57,800 --> 00:32:59,208
Yes, Grandma.

378
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:33,881
Yes, Grandma?

379
00:33:33,881 --> 00:33:38,670
Yai, if you're not too busy,
come see me at home,

380
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:40,480
right away.

381
00:33:51,393 --> 00:33:57,988
♪ Though the earth and sky may perish ♪

382
00:33:57,988 --> 00:34:05,233
♪ My love for you is unwavering ♪

383
00:34:05,233 --> 00:34:12,451
♪ Wherever we may be born ♪

384
00:34:12,451 --> 00:34:19,873
♪ May we reunite in love, never to part ♪

385
00:34:19,873 --> 00:34:25,883
♪ If you were the great ocean ♪

386
00:34:26,610 --> 00:34:34,340
♪ I'd be a fish to swim within ♪

387
00:34:34,340 --> 00:34:40,910
♪ If you were a lotus, I'd be a bee ♪

388
00:34:40,910 --> 00:34:47,660
♪ Forever drawn to the golden bloom ♪

389
00:34:48,290 --> 00:34:55,000
♪ Even if you were a radiant grotto ♪

390
00:34:55,000 --> 00:35:03,800
♪ I'd fly down as a swan to dwell within ♪

391
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:11,057
♪ I shall be ever by your side ♪

392
00:35:11,057 --> 00:35:18,447
♪ Your beloved in every lifetime ♪

393
00:35:25,378 --> 00:35:27,667
Oh, Yai, you're here.

394
00:35:29,904 --> 00:35:31,182
Yes.

395
00:35:35,058 --> 00:35:38,920
Dao, you've met Yai before, haven't you?

396
00:35:38,920 --> 00:35:43,570
I have. But there's always
some trouble whenever we meet.

397
00:35:44,448 --> 00:35:47,964
And whose fault is that?
You were such a rascal.

398
00:35:49,600 --> 00:35:51,480
How do you greet your senior?

399
00:35:51,480 --> 00:35:52,750
Hello.

400
00:35:54,040 --> 00:35:56,425
What do you want to talk to me about, Grandma?

401
00:36:00,761 --> 00:36:02,167
What is this?

402
00:36:03,404 --> 00:36:07,200
This is Dao's hair. I styled her hair earlier.

403
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:09,120
Use this to test her DNA.

404
00:36:11,200 --> 00:36:12,346
Grandma.

405
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:16,640
How did you know?

406
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:18,360
I know everything.

407
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:20,820
Who is who. Who did what.

408
00:36:22,985 --> 00:36:24,860
It's not like you think.

409
00:36:24,860 --> 00:36:28,357
I had an investigator check.
Dao isn't my daughter.

410
00:36:28,357 --> 00:36:33,062
But I don't think it's a coincidence
that I met Dao.

411
00:36:33,062 --> 00:36:34,920
There has to be a reason.

412
00:36:34,920 --> 00:36:39,884
And I won't give up until I know the truth.

413
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:42,446
Grandma...

414
00:36:43,320 --> 00:36:48,196
Answer me,
have you already given it your all?

415
00:36:51,953 --> 00:36:53,119
No.

416
00:36:53,726 --> 00:36:56,056
We'll talk after you get the results.

417
00:36:59,173 --> 00:37:00,173
Oh.

418
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:04,880
Did Lek tell you that Dao looks...

419
00:37:04,880 --> 00:37:07,120
exactly like me when I was younger?

420
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:10,510
Hearing that, how could I not have hope?

421
00:37:12,120 --> 00:37:13,920
Don't get your hopes up.

422
00:37:15,001 --> 00:37:18,000
Well, I'm expecting good news.

423
00:37:24,068 --> 00:37:25,646
Are they tasty?

424
00:37:39,086 --> 00:37:42,375
You're actually pretty kind,
driving me home like this.

425
00:37:43,520 --> 00:37:47,150
But if you smile more,
you'll definitely attract many more women.

426
00:37:47,150 --> 00:37:48,758
They'll swarm around you.

427
00:37:50,282 --> 00:37:53,609
Why do I feel like I'm a pile of poop?

428
00:37:58,580 --> 00:38:00,291
Don't be so stiff.

429
00:38:00,291 --> 00:38:01,533
We're almost there.

430
00:38:02,240 --> 00:38:04,000
Okay.

431
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:05,919
Have you ever asked your mother

432
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:08,966
why she named you Dao?

433
00:38:09,592 --> 00:38:13,440
I have. Mom said my sister gave me that name.

434
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:15,440
When I asked her,

435
00:38:16,506 --> 00:38:18,289
she said,

436
00:38:19,671 --> 00:38:22,828
"Because you are the light that guides me."

437
00:38:28,040 --> 00:38:29,151
And...

438
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:31,383
what's your real name?

439
00:38:32,080 --> 00:38:34,205
My name is Daranee.

440
00:38:34,205 --> 00:38:35,960
It means stars.

441
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:39,640
She said my name means
the woman from the stars.

442
00:38:47,400 --> 00:38:48,963
We'll get married

443
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:51,400
and have kids together, Ran.

444
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:56,626
If we have a daughter, I'll name her Dao,

445
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:01,856
because the stars are prettier
than usual today.

446
00:39:14,301 --> 00:39:16,448
And what about you, Uncle?

447
00:39:18,107 --> 00:39:19,852
Stop calling me that.

448
00:39:19,852 --> 00:39:21,637
Be happy I didn't call you Gramps.

449
00:39:21,637 --> 00:39:22,657
Oops.

450
00:39:23,600 --> 00:39:26,200
Sorry. I didn't mean to think out loud.

451
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:29,600
Just call me Uncle.

452
00:39:30,640 --> 00:39:32,595
But an uncle has to be older than my dad.

453
00:39:32,595 --> 00:39:34,800
My dad is a lot older than you.

454
00:39:34,800 --> 00:39:36,040
You can call me Uncle.

455
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:40,440
I'm fine with both Uncle Yai
and Uncle Rangsiman.

456
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:43,519
It has to be Uncle Yai.
Uncle Rangsiman is too lengthy.

457
00:39:44,200 --> 00:39:45,720
And...

458
00:39:45,720 --> 00:39:47,635
what does Rangsiman mean?

459
00:39:47,635 --> 00:39:50,356
"Rangsiman" means the sun.

460
00:39:50,356 --> 00:39:52,136
My grandmother gave me that name.

461
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:58,280
Come to think of it, we're both
in the sky, just at different times.

462
00:39:58,280 --> 00:40:01,720
I'm up there at night,
while you're up there in the day.

463
00:40:01,720 --> 00:40:03,400
But I'm not jealous.

464
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:05,865
The night has so many stars,

465
00:40:05,865 --> 00:40:09,535
while the sun is alone in the day. It's lonely.

466
00:40:12,226 --> 00:40:16,022
Uncle Yai, can I ask you
to give my gifts to Sam for me?

467
00:40:16,022 --> 00:40:17,357
Of course.

468
00:40:17,357 --> 00:40:20,872
You can text me whenever
you have something to give him.

469
00:40:20,872 --> 00:40:22,194
But how?

470
00:40:22,194 --> 00:40:24,674
I don't have your number or your contact info.

471
00:40:25,840 --> 00:40:28,614
Here. Let's exchange contacts.

472
00:40:34,498 --> 00:40:37,348
- I can text you anytime?
- Mm.

473
00:40:38,200 --> 00:40:39,640
That's great!

474
00:40:57,160 --> 00:41:01,471
Thank you, Uncle Yai. I'm going now. Goodbye.

475
00:41:32,690 --> 00:41:34,707
Dao! What happened?

476
00:41:34,707 --> 00:41:37,002
My savings are all gone.

477
00:41:37,840 --> 00:41:40,377
It's definitely Danai's doing!

478
00:41:53,560 --> 00:41:55,044
Danai.

479
00:41:58,913 --> 00:42:00,627
Did you steal Dao's money?

480
00:42:01,323 --> 00:42:03,113
Sis, I had to.

481
00:42:03,113 --> 00:42:04,320
What do you mean?

482
00:42:07,360 --> 00:42:09,433
If I don't give them money,

483
00:42:09,433 --> 00:42:11,214
they're going to kill me.

484
00:42:11,214 --> 00:42:14,237
- They're going to kill me, Sis.
- Who's going to kill you?

485
00:42:15,908 --> 00:42:17,823
It's the loan sharks.

486
00:42:19,375 --> 00:42:21,174
I was addicted to online gambling,

487
00:42:21,800 --> 00:42:23,366
so I borrowed money from them.

488
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:27,560
They said, if I don't pay them back,

489
00:42:27,560 --> 00:42:29,135
they're going to kill me.

490
00:42:33,040 --> 00:42:34,620
Why did you get into gambling?

491
00:42:34,620 --> 00:42:38,220
Didn't I tell you to never gamble? Danai!

492
00:42:38,220 --> 00:42:39,970
- Why are you like this?
- Ran, enough.

493
00:42:39,970 --> 00:42:42,210
- Why did you do that?
- Stop, you're hurting him.

494
00:42:42,210 --> 00:42:44,070
- Stop.
- I'm sorry.

495
00:42:45,741 --> 00:42:47,500
I'm sorry.

496
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:53,400
I just wanted to make some money.

497
00:42:53,400 --> 00:42:55,485
At first, it worked.

498
00:42:56,920 --> 00:42:59,884
But who would've known
I'd lose so much money?

499
00:43:07,222 --> 00:43:08,977
I'm sorry, Sis.

500
00:43:10,550 --> 00:43:13,400
If it were that easy to make money,

501
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:15,640
I would've done it already.

502
00:43:15,640 --> 00:43:18,516
Why would I have to work day and night, then?

503
00:43:20,360 --> 00:43:23,480
Your sister saved up her money.

504
00:43:23,480 --> 00:43:25,445
You broke her heart.

505
00:43:29,219 --> 00:43:31,516
Well, it's because you bought Dao

506
00:43:31,516 --> 00:43:33,687
whatever she asked for!

507
00:43:34,400 --> 00:43:35,955
What about me?

508
00:43:35,955 --> 00:43:37,820
What have you even bought for me?

509
00:43:38,512 --> 00:43:40,800
You didn't even buy me

510
00:43:40,800 --> 00:43:42,502
a single pair of shoes!

511
00:43:42,502 --> 00:43:45,330
I asked you before, but you said no!

512
00:43:45,330 --> 00:43:47,420
I felt bad for you.

513
00:43:48,417 --> 00:43:50,920
Shouldn't you be able to figure out

514
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:52,961
what I used to get?

515
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:58,038
You don't care about me.

516
00:43:58,038 --> 00:44:01,763
Yeah, I'm an idiot! I'm not a genius like you!

517
00:44:02,520 --> 00:44:06,280
But what kind of genius
can't stop herself from getting pregnant!

518
00:44:06,280 --> 00:44:08,313
Oh dear!

519
00:44:17,367 --> 00:44:18,696
Danai...

520
00:45:01,160 --> 00:45:03,269
I feel bad for him, Mom.

521
00:45:05,003 --> 00:45:06,743
I never knew

522
00:45:07,557 --> 00:45:10,050
he'd been feeling so overlooked.

523
00:45:14,588 --> 00:45:17,019
I didn't know either.

524
00:45:18,212 --> 00:45:21,714
It seems like we forgot to think about Danai.

525
00:45:24,430 --> 00:45:26,159
He must have been lonely

526
00:45:27,241 --> 00:45:29,894
and didn't have anyone to talk to, Mom.

527
00:45:32,603 --> 00:45:34,261
It's my fault.

528
00:45:38,760 --> 00:45:40,253
I'm in the wrong, too.

529
00:46:14,079 --> 00:46:16,154
I'm sorry, Danai.

530
00:46:21,388 --> 00:46:23,065
I'm sorry.

531
00:46:25,565 --> 00:46:27,448
I'm just jealous of Dao.

532
00:46:30,313 --> 00:46:31,933
Ever since you had Dao,

533
00:46:32,723 --> 00:46:34,706
you only care about her.

534
00:46:35,709 --> 00:46:37,995
Everyone only cares about her.

535
00:46:41,300 --> 00:46:43,360
Sometimes I just think...

536
00:46:43,360 --> 00:46:45,340
why wasn't I born as your son?

537
00:46:58,122 --> 00:47:00,354
Next time, just tell me what's wrong.

538
00:47:00,932 --> 00:47:02,916
Sometimes I have no idea.

539
00:47:05,008 --> 00:47:06,572
And I'll help find the money

540
00:47:07,454 --> 00:47:09,518
to pay off your gambling debt.

541
00:47:10,413 --> 00:47:13,252
But you have to promise me
that you won't do it again.

542
00:47:46,460 --> 00:47:49,460
[MJTV]

543
00:47:55,631 --> 00:47:57,240
Where's Daran?

544
00:47:57,240 --> 00:47:58,887
She resigned, sir.

545
00:47:58,887 --> 00:48:00,208
Huh?

546
00:48:06,480 --> 00:48:08,040
Why didn't you stop her?

547
00:48:08,040 --> 00:48:10,000
If she can't find work, how will she survive?

548
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:13,360
Huh?

549
00:48:14,440 --> 00:48:15,940
I don't know, sir.

550
00:48:17,714 --> 00:48:19,634
The one who let her resign is here.

551
00:48:20,240 --> 00:48:21,800
You may ask him directly, sir.

552
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:23,030
What's wrong?

553
00:48:25,044 --> 00:48:26,901
Who fired Daran?

554
00:48:26,901 --> 00:48:29,153
I need an answer. Now!

555
00:48:30,640 --> 00:48:32,380
Answer me!

556
00:48:38,458 --> 00:48:41,360
If it's not work-related,
don't let Sam come see me anymore.

557
00:48:41,360 --> 00:48:42,686
Why, sir?

558
00:48:42,686 --> 00:48:43,713
He's annoying.

559
00:48:46,800 --> 00:48:48,420
Lek, too.

560
00:48:48,420 --> 00:48:50,040
Mr. Lek too?

561
00:48:51,400 --> 00:48:54,231
Bring the meeting agenda to my office.

562
00:49:06,933 --> 00:49:08,301
Have a seat.

563
00:49:12,583 --> 00:49:16,471
Thank you for taking my call
and coming to see me.

564
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:20,494
What do you want to talk to me about?

565
00:49:21,680 --> 00:49:23,432
Why did you resign?

566
00:49:25,480 --> 00:49:28,350
Didn't you say you had
something important to talk about?

567
00:49:29,342 --> 00:49:30,867
This is what I wanted to talk about.

568
00:49:30,867 --> 00:49:32,847
If you resign,

569
00:49:32,847 --> 00:49:34,611
you'll have to live somewhere else.

570
00:49:35,240 --> 00:49:37,680
Money is also important.

571
00:49:37,680 --> 00:49:39,700
Without an income,

572
00:49:39,700 --> 00:49:41,380
your family would struggle,

573
00:49:42,259 --> 00:49:44,840
and you'd be in serious trouble.

574
00:49:44,840 --> 00:49:46,320
Then...

575
00:49:47,760 --> 00:49:49,447
do you want to work with me?

576
00:49:53,440 --> 00:49:54,880
So...

577
00:49:54,880 --> 00:49:58,469
I'm not pitying you or anything,

578
00:49:58,469 --> 00:50:02,010
but my artist relations staff just resigned,

579
00:50:02,010 --> 00:50:03,540
so I'm looking for a replacement.

580
00:50:05,360 --> 00:50:06,770
What a coincidence.

581
00:50:07,520 --> 00:50:10,485
Right. Quite a coincidence.

582
00:50:10,485 --> 00:50:14,470
Anyway, you can manage your
work schedule however you like.

583
00:50:15,040 --> 00:50:17,300
As for the salary, I'll give you 50,000.

584
00:50:18,520 --> 00:50:20,360
That's too much.

585
00:50:20,360 --> 00:50:22,960
I... couldn't accept that.

586
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:26,460
So if it's less than that,
you'd accept it, right?

587
00:50:28,600 --> 00:50:31,329
Then I'll give you 35,000 baht.

588
00:50:31,329 --> 00:50:32,840
Please accept it, Auntie.

589
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:35,258
Once you find a new job,
we can talk about it again.

590
00:50:40,140 --> 00:50:42,700
This is already quite low.

591
00:50:42,700 --> 00:50:45,402
This job is very time-consuming.

592
00:50:45,402 --> 00:50:48,160
Others normally get paid a lot more.

593
00:50:49,352 --> 00:50:51,652
I'll think about it, then.

594
00:50:52,720 --> 00:50:56,574
But still... Thank you so much.

595
00:51:06,600 --> 00:51:07,838
Okay.

596
00:51:16,810 --> 00:51:18,160
Ran.

597
00:51:18,160 --> 00:51:22,022
Don't take this the wrong way,
but why did you make that decision?

598
00:51:22,022 --> 00:51:23,702
You don't even have a new job yet.

599
00:51:25,630 --> 00:51:26,820
I'm scared, Mom.

600
00:51:27,560 --> 00:51:28,934
What are you scared of?

601
00:51:30,360 --> 00:51:32,880
Yai is getting too close to my life.

602
00:51:32,880 --> 00:51:34,920
I'm scared that if he finds out,

603
00:51:34,920 --> 00:51:36,533
it'll throw our family into chaos.

604
00:52:05,260 --> 00:52:09,070
[Mr. Ronnaphob]

605
00:52:57,904 --> 00:53:00,013
Why hasn't she called me?

606
00:53:01,760 --> 00:53:03,640
I want to help Ran,

607
00:53:03,640 --> 00:53:07,040
but she doesn't want my help,
which I understand.

608
00:53:09,020 --> 00:53:11,600
You're the only one who can help her now.

609
00:53:12,280 --> 00:53:14,380
- Are you stepping aside?
- No.

610
00:53:15,120 --> 00:53:18,599
You have to take care of Ran for Yai.

611
00:53:20,120 --> 00:53:22,435
That's not what I had in mind, though.

612
00:53:27,400 --> 00:53:29,120
Just kidding.

613
00:53:29,120 --> 00:53:31,325
Since you trust me,

614
00:53:31,325 --> 00:53:33,180
I won't disappoint you.

615
00:53:33,920 --> 00:53:35,650
I already know...

616
00:53:35,650 --> 00:53:37,985
that Yai still loves Ran.

617
00:53:40,598 --> 00:53:41,713
This time,

618
00:53:43,044 --> 00:53:44,674
I'll take one for the team.

619
00:53:45,520 --> 00:53:46,689
Thank you so much.

620
00:53:47,549 --> 00:53:48,960
Wait.

621
00:53:48,960 --> 00:53:50,960
But if Auntie fell in love with me,

622
00:53:52,400 --> 00:53:54,338
I can't help that, though.

623
00:53:57,240 --> 00:53:58,721
You don't believe me?

624
00:54:00,010 --> 00:54:02,697
Okay. Let's try it.

625
00:54:10,760 --> 00:54:14,010
[My dear auntie zombie]

626
00:54:20,147 --> 00:54:21,467
Hello.

627
00:54:22,225 --> 00:54:23,506
Please come in.

628
00:54:30,016 --> 00:54:31,717
Have some water first.

629
00:54:32,667 --> 00:54:33,818
Thank you.

630
00:54:35,664 --> 00:54:37,059
Don't worry.

631
00:54:37,059 --> 00:54:40,339
Now that you work with me,
you'll have to come to my condo sometimes,

632
00:54:40,339 --> 00:54:42,162
because I might not wake up on time.

633
00:54:45,120 --> 00:54:47,311
Here's the keycard.

634
00:54:54,282 --> 00:54:56,701
Can I give you a little makeover?

635
00:54:59,210 --> 00:55:00,500
This way, please.

636
00:55:12,131 --> 00:55:13,861
Turn around.

637
00:55:16,186 --> 00:55:17,746
Okay.

638
00:55:26,840 --> 00:55:27,933
Okay.

639
00:55:27,933 --> 00:55:30,120
Let's try the third one.

640
00:55:48,210 --> 00:55:50,440
Approved.

641
00:55:50,440 --> 00:55:53,640
I don't think I'm well suited for this job.

642
00:55:53,640 --> 00:55:56,000
This is more stressful
than being a security guard.

643
00:55:56,000 --> 00:55:57,879
Why do you think that?

644
00:55:57,879 --> 00:55:59,523
You haven't even tried it.

645
00:56:01,077 --> 00:56:03,675
Everything... takes time to learn.

646
00:56:04,576 --> 00:56:07,189
Nobody has experience...

647
00:56:08,177 --> 00:56:10,145
before they start working!

648
00:56:11,408 --> 00:56:13,088
Well, that's true.

649
00:56:13,720 --> 00:56:17,835
Usually, my manager
will take care of me all day.

650
00:56:17,835 --> 00:56:20,330
But as my artist relations staff,

651
00:56:20,330 --> 00:56:24,480
you'll start working and finish
at the same time as me.

652
00:56:24,480 --> 00:56:28,430
You'll go to work sites,
events, and filming sets.

653
00:56:28,430 --> 00:56:31,299
Some days, you'll have to wake up very early

654
00:56:31,299 --> 00:56:33,190
and work until 1 or 2 a.m.

655
00:56:33,190 --> 00:56:35,730
But if you work more than
12 hours on any day,

656
00:56:35,730 --> 00:56:37,380
I'll count that as overtime.

657
00:56:38,520 --> 00:56:41,388
And if I don't have any work on a given day,

658
00:56:41,388 --> 00:56:43,163
you can just stay at home.

659
00:56:43,163 --> 00:56:45,118
That's your free time.

660
00:56:45,118 --> 00:56:48,014
If you have something to take care of,
you can take the day off.

661
00:56:48,014 --> 00:56:49,500
Don't worry about me.

662
00:56:49,500 --> 00:56:52,117
Is there anything you'd like to ask?

663
00:56:55,920 --> 00:56:57,880
I only have one condition.

664
00:56:57,880 --> 00:56:59,400
Say it.

665
00:56:59,400 --> 00:57:01,641
I won't go to MJTV Station.

666
00:57:06,831 --> 00:57:08,242
Deal.

667
00:57:10,077 --> 00:57:11,406
Deal.

668
00:57:17,146 --> 00:57:19,123
The DNA test report is here.

669
00:57:34,013 --> 00:57:35,999
[Rangsiman Metharavee cannot
be excluded as Daranee's father.]

670
00:57:35,999 --> 00:57:38,353
[The paternity test shows
a 99.99% probability of paternity.]

671
00:57:48,386 --> 00:57:51,193
Lek, do you know where Daran is?

672
00:57:55,065 --> 00:57:57,568
I have ten minutes
before I shoot the music video.

673
00:57:58,493 --> 00:58:00,515
I have something to tell you.

674
00:58:00,515 --> 00:58:01,600
Okay.

675
00:58:03,217 --> 00:58:05,084
I'm going to be serious now.

676
00:58:06,869 --> 00:58:08,396
I'm waiting.

677
00:58:12,200 --> 00:58:14,029
Yai still loves you.

678
00:58:17,789 --> 00:58:20,040
I've known Yai...

679
00:58:20,040 --> 00:58:21,880
since he was studying in the US.

680
00:58:22,721 --> 00:58:25,263
He was totally devastated.

681
00:58:26,080 --> 00:58:27,912
He was never interested in anyone.

682
00:58:28,520 --> 00:58:30,240
Even Nana,

683
00:58:30,240 --> 00:58:33,875
who'd waited over ten years for him
could never make him change his mind.

684
00:58:35,280 --> 00:58:37,371
But as soon as you resigned,

685
00:58:38,480 --> 00:58:42,566
Yai became really worried
that you might have a hard time.

686
00:58:45,487 --> 00:58:47,293
From what I can see,

687
00:58:49,674 --> 00:58:52,801
he still loves you, Ms. Daran.

688
00:58:54,800 --> 00:58:56,904
He loves you more than anyone.

689
00:59:21,825 --> 00:59:23,154
Ran.

690
00:59:34,550 --> 00:59:36,550
I know our child is alive.

691
00:59:49,420 --> 00:59:51,120
This is the DNA result for Dao and me.

692
00:59:51,120 --> 00:59:52,690
She'd never accept it if she knew...

693
00:59:52,690 --> 00:59:55,460
she was born to irresponsible parents.

694
00:59:56,180 --> 00:59:58,227
[Daranee Kaewkaruna]
What are you to Daran?

695
00:59:59,120 --> 01:00:00,830
Have you ever had a boyfriend?

696
01:00:00,830 --> 01:00:01,863
I have.

697
01:00:01,863 --> 01:00:04,120
And where is he now?

698
01:00:04,120 --> 01:00:05,960
Has Ran gotten pregnant before?

699
01:00:05,960 --> 01:00:08,200
I could reach her,
but she turned off her phone.

700
01:00:08,200 --> 01:00:11,326
The body of an unidentified teenage girl
was found drowned beneath a bridge.
